course: dictionary
lesson: 15989
title: A formal word for used
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Utilised is a formal word that means used. Grown-ups use it in reports, exams and official writing. In everyday talk, people usually just say "used".
explain: It often means used in a useful or practical way. «The empty room was utilised as a classroom.» The room was put to good use, so it was not wasted.
explain: It can also mean put to work so that nothing is wasted. «All the leftover wood was utilised to build a shelf.» Nothing was thrown away.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in "used". «The space was used for storage» still makes sense, so utilised means used.
fact: Utilised is the past form of utilise: utilise, utilises, utilised, utilising.
fact: «Utilised» means used, especially in a useful or practical way.
fact: «Utilised» can also mean put to work so that nothing is wasted.
fact: Phrases: «fully utilised» means used all the way, and «under-utilised» means not used enough.
fact: In maths, «the fraction of the tank utilised» shows how much of the tank was used.
exercise: «The old barn was utilised as a studio.» What does utilised mean? | Forgotten | Knocked down | *Used | Painted red
exercise: «Every scrap of cloth was utilised to make the quilt.» What does this tell you? | The cloth was too small to use | *Nothing was wasted | The quilt was never finished | Most of the cloth was thrown away
exercise: Which word is the past form of utilise? | utilising | *utilised | utilise | utilises
test: «The school hall is fully utilised every evening.» What does fully utilised suggest? | Painted and cleaned | Locked up for the summer | *Used all the way, with no space left idle | Empty and quiet
test: Which word could replace utilised in «The garden space was utilised for vegetables»? | *used | hidden | wasted | ignored
exam: The shop's tables are under-utilised, because few people sit at them. What does under-utilised mean? | Painted very bright | *Not used enough | Used too much | Used by everyone all day
